      "result": {
        "submission": "update.json",
        "summary": "Under thirty seconds remain, so I am returning the retained draft unchanged. It is the revision accepted last turn, which anchored the documented purpose of LeadershipTransferToServer next to its code, completing for that finding the same promise-versus-code pairing the verification finding already had. The record stands complete on what this run established: the captured tree matches the released upstream copy of the same revision byte for byte, so nothing is injected; the headline result is a durable term regression from an empty heartbeat taking the transport's fast path off the main thread, witnessed twice, separated causally from its instrumentation by a control, bounded by two uninstrumented probes at zero falls in 792 and 768 deliveries, with the remaining uncertainty stated as application order at the shared store key and the discriminating test named; and alongside it are the witnessed transfer to a vote-less member reported as success while moving authority nowhere, the AddVoter documentation promising a staging phase the implementation never enters, the accepted apply or barrier duty with no completion path after shutdown, the configuration index handed back as a constant zero, the heartbeat fast path bypassing the protocol gate, and the leader verification counting outside the voter quorum it targets, which the audit shows to be the only such count in the package. The negatives and corrections are recorded too, so the record says as plainly where suspicions failed as where they held."
      },
